

# (Enable this template for all commits in this project with "git config commit.template .gitmessage".)
# (Otherwise specify "-t .gitmessage" with "git commit" and do not add "-m" or "-F" to use it one-time.)

# Write a short summary of the changes you have made on the first line.

# Add additional context, that cannot be inferred from the first line, as multiple
# lines after a newline. Include as much information as needed to let others understand
# the purpose of this commit but without adding too much unrelated bloat.
# State why the change was made when the change itself does not say so.
# For example, explain acronyms when they are not obvious for fairly new users.
# But refrain from explaining well-known acronyms.
# The acronym "OPDS" (Open Publication Distribution System) needs an explanation, but "JSON" does not.

# Note anything a user or an operator would notice in CHANGELOG.md as well,
# under "Unreleased", and mark an upgrade that needs action with "BREAKING".


## AI Agents
# Specify when AI Agents, LLMs or similar where used to create parts or the whole commit.
# When using Claude Code in a terminal with Opus 5, uncomment the two lines below.
#
#AI-Agent: Anthropic Claude Code (v2.1/CLI)
#AI-Model: Anthropic Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
#
# Otherwise, fill the following in and uncomment them:
#
#AI-Agent: Company Product (Version/Environment)
#AI-Model: Company Model Version (model-api-identifier)
#
# If more than one agent or model was used, add one trailer pair per agent and model.
#
# Why AI-Agent?
# This allows others to know and understand what tool you used.
# If you use Claude Code in a Terminal, the text "Anthropic Claude Code (v2.1.141/CLI)" lets others know that.
# Example for OpenCode in VS Code: "Anomaly OpenCode (v1.14.48/Visual Studio Code)".
#
# Why AI-Model?
# Since nearly every Agent supports multiple models and each model behaving differently,
# knowing the model becomes important. The API Identifier helps others select the same model.
# If you use Sonnet 5, the text "Anthropic Claude Sonnet 5 (claude-sonnet-5)" gives that information.
# Example for Gemini 3: "Google Gemini 3 Flash (gemini-3-flash-preview)"
#
# Do NOT include the Agent via an "Co-Authored-By".
# That one should be reserved for human co-authors, not tools/programs/LLMs.
# See MACHINE_POLICY.md, sections 7.2.5 and 7.2.6.
